# {{name}}

{{description}}

A [Rustic](https://github.com/Rustic-Launcher/server) plugin (template: `{{template}}`).

## Develop

```sh
rustic build          # compile to wasm32-wasip2, validate, package target/rustic/{{id}}.rplugin
rustic test           # run the tests: the real .wasm in an in-memory server
rustic run            # try it: a dev server, or a REPL (join Steve, chat Steve hi, tick 20...)
rustic run --watch    # rebuild and hot-reload on save
rustic check          # manifest, API version, capabilities, imports
rustic package        # release build, ready to upload
```

## Install

Copy `target/rustic/{{id}}.rplugin` into the server's `plugins/` folder and restart (or run
`/rustic reload {{id}}` when updating). The default `config.toml` is copied to
`plugins/{{id}}/config.toml` on first start.

## Layout

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `rustic.plugin.toml` | manifest: id, version, API, capabilities |
| `config.toml` | default configuration (admins edit their copy) |
| `src/lib.rs` | the plugin |
| `tests/` | integration tests with `rusticmc-test` |
